===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form|cat2=irregular past participles}}

# {{inflection of|en|go||past|part}}
# {{alternative spelling of|en|gon}} or [[gon']]: short for [[gonna]], [[going to]].
#* {{RQ:Noire Thug-A-Licious|page=24|passage=Take or be taken. Get yours or get got. It was the code of the streets and I'd lived by it. The way things was looking, I was prolly '''gone''' die by it too.}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|further|er}}

# [[away|Away]], having left.
#: {{ux|en|Are they '''gone''' already?}}
# No longer [[existing]], having [[passed]].
#: {{ux|en|The days of my youth are '''gone'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|All the little shops that used to be here are now '''gone'''.}}
# [[used up|Used up]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm afraid all the coffee's '''gone''' at the moment.}}
#: {{ux|en|The bulb's '''gone''', can you put a new one in?.}}
# [[dead|Dead]].
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=221|volume=I|passage=Dust, that a breath could blow aside, yet that was once, like ourselves, animate with hope, passion, and sorrow, is below; around are the vain memorials of human grief and human pride; yet all alike dedicated to the '''gone'''.}}
# [[doomed|Doomed]], [[done for]].
#: {{ux|en|Have you seen the company's revenue? It's [[through the floor]]. They're '''gone'''.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} Not fully [[aware]] of one's surroundings, often through [[intoxication]] or mental [[decline]].
#: {{ux|en|Don't bother trying to understand what Grandma says; she's '''gone'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|page=28|passage={{...}}she put on a kind of sing-song voice whenever she was pissed, it was one of the signs that she was really '''gone'''{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} Entirely given up to; [[infatuated]] with; used with ''on''.
#: {{ux|en|He's totally '''gone''' on her.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|US|dated}} [[excellent|Excellent]], [[wonderful]]; [[crazy]].
#: {{ux|en|It was a group of real '''gone''' cats.}}
#* {{RQ:Kerouac On the Road|part=1|chapter=11|page=61|year_published=1976|passage=“All right, all right, don’t drop your gold all over the place. I have found the '''gonest''' little girl in the world and I am going straight to the Lion’s Den with her tonight.”}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1975|writers={{w|Garry Marshall}} et al.|title={{w|Happy Days}}|episode=Richie's Flip Side|season=2|number=21|role={{w|Richie Cunningham}}|actor=Ron Howard|passage=Dad, I want to be a jock. All a jock needs is some hep patter and a real '''gone''' image. Now, they just don't teach that jazz in college.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[ago|Ago]] {{non-gloss definition|(used post-positionally)}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1999|author={{w|George R.R. Martin}}|title=A Clash of Kings|page=491|publisher=Bantam|year_published=2011
|passage=Six nights '''gone''', your brother fell upon my uncle Stafford, encamped with his host at a village called Oxcross not three days ride from Casterly Rock.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} [[weak|Weak]]; [[faint]]; feeling a sense of [[goneness]].
# Of an arrow: [[wide of the mark]].
# {{non-gloss definition|Used with a genitively constructed duration to indicate for how long a process has been developing, an action has been performed or a state has persisted}}; [[pregnant]].
#: {{ux|en|She’s three months' '''gone'''
}}

